{"name":"Fresh Zest","hex":"#f5e9cf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fresh","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Newly produced or obtained; recent.","(of food) Not dried, frozen, or spoiled."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Recently; just recently; most recently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fresh"},{"term":"zest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The outer skin of a citrus fruit, used as a flavouring or garnish.","General vibrance of flavour."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To scrape the zest from a fruit.","To make more zesty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Zest (ingredient)","blocks":[{"text":"Zest is a food ingredient that is prepared by scraping or cutting from the rind of unwaxed citrus fruits such as lemon, orange, citron, and lime. Zest is used to add flavor to many different types of food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Zesting_an_orange.jpg/330px-Zesting_an_orange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zest_(ingredient)","wikidata":"Q196819"},{"title":"Zest (brand)","blocks":[{"text":"Zest is an American brand of soap and body wash owned by Sodalis USA for the United States, Canada, and Puerto Rico and by Unilever for the rest of the world. It was initially introduced by Procter & Gamble in 1955 with the slogan \"For the first time in your life, feel really clean.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Zest_logo.svg/330px-Zest_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zest_(brand)","wikidata":"Q8069689"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Juliennejern.JPG/500px-Juliennejern.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia